{{!--
  cargo-about 0.9.2 Handlebars template for THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.

  The release workflow renders this template's output to
  "$RUNNER_TEMP/notices.body" and writes its own header (release, commit,
  artifact, generator version, and the root crate's Required Notice line)
  above it. This file therefore contains only the third-party body.

  Template data (cargo_about::generate::LicenseList):
    overview  - one entry per licence id, with count/name/id/text
    licenses  - one entry per unique licence *text*; fields name, id,
                first_of_kind, text, source_path, used_by
    used_by   - entries with `crate` (a cargo_metadata Package) and `path`

  `source_path` is deliberately not rendered: it is an absolute path into the
  build machine's cargo registry (`/home/runner/.cargo/...` on CI, a different
  path on every other machine), so printing it would put a machine-specific
  location the recipient cannot check into a consumer-facing document. The
  licence text itself is rendered in full below.
--}}
THIRD-PARTY LICENCE SUMMARY
===========================

{{#each overview}}
{{{name}}} ({{id}}): {{count}} crate(s)
{{/each}}

The full text of each licence follows. A licence text that is shared by more
than one crate is printed once, with every crate it applies to listed beneath
it. Crates are listed by the name and version recorded in Cargo.lock.
{{#each licenses}}

================================================================================
{{{name}}} ({{id}})
================================================================================

Applies to:
{{#each used_by}}
  * {{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}{{#if crate.repository}} <{{{crate.repository}}}>{{/if}}
{{/each}}

{{{text}}}
{{/each}}
